    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0996" n="1504" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/10–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Egypt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-21T19:00:00-05:00">October 21, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1455. Dept considers security of ME would probably
                    be strengthened if large part Arab Palestine were incorporated in Transjordan
                    after satisfactory solution problem demarcation Arab-Israel frontiers reached
                    through UN (ur 1485 Oct 13). We agree however that continued <pb facs="0997"
                        n="1505" xml:id="pg1505"/> Brit insistence on merging Arab Palestine with
                    Transjordan may have adverse effects Arab capitals.</p>
                <p>Dept would not object to acquisition by Egypt small portion of Arab Palestine, in
                    line with Mediator’s conclusion 4–<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>. However, Egypt
                    has apparently so far shown no desire to do so. We believe it preferable that
                    matter be raised by Egypt on own initiative and independently.</p>
                <p>Re final para reftel, while Bernadotte may
                    have held views in Aug as reported ur 1105 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1103–A</hi>],<anchor n="1" xml:id="d690-f1"/> he definitely on Sep 14
                    rejected UK suggestion that Syria profit by partition of Arab Palestine.
                    Bernadotte also applied same reasoning to Lebanon. Foregoing for your info
                        only.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d690-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d690-f1" n="1" xml:id="d690-f1-content">
